Expose bucket-key encryption for internal recipients (Hylki)

Confidential (end-to-end encrypted) Tuta-to-Tuta mail needs the bucket key
encrypted with each recipient's public key, which only the SDK's
AsymmetricCryptoFacade can do -- and LoggedInSdk does not expose it.

This adds AsymmetricCryptoFacade::encrypt_bucket_key_for_internal_recipients,
the internal-recipient arm of the TS MailFacade.addRecipientKeyData and
CryptoFacade.encryptBucketKeyForInternalRecipient: current public keys come
from the PublicKeyService through the PublicKeyProvider, asym_encrypt_sym_key
encrypts (legacy RSA, or TutaCrypt with the sender identity key, created first
when the sender group has none), unknown recipients are collected and fail
the whole set. LoggedInSdk keeps the facade it already builds and exposes the
call, choosing the sender key group as the TS client does (the user group, or
a shared mailbox's own). Each result carries a SHA-256 fingerprint of the key
it used, so a caller can pin keys. No cryptography is added; only existing SDK
primitives are composed.

